gned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417378 1072 #uuid "b47d0cc7-71aa-58ba-a792-0650346f33fc" 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417378 1074 "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417379 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417375 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417379 1069 "q-131383" 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417379 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417379 1071 "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $D$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${D}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 &  &  \\\\ 0 & 1 &  & \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417379 1072 #uuid "bcd8ebdd-840f-56b3-b01b-b55941f100d8" 13194139534285 17592186045417 true] [17592186417379 1074 "We write down $D$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $D$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${D}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{D}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534285 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-05827898-9cd0-5481-9f4f-2795de94047f" 17592186417360 "answer-0fb31cbb-95b7-5502-b5a4-6f06608e01c1" 17592186417361 "answer-27195729-1b10-59a4-9a7d-c8f3fb5b730d" 17592186417362 "answer-30ffe217-9ca4-5886-8537-db99704507c9" 17592186417363 "answer-351e7f30-9491-58fc-8cf5-793274bcf323" 17592186417364 "answer-36ed8b6e-c128-5d01-928b-08f774f8d809" 17592186417365 "answer-41d70487-8623-57c9-b21d-be91769cf161" 17592186417366 "answer-482e772e-15aa-5a49-ba61-a3210d49dce1" 17592186417367 "answer-5daf2709-08dc-5216-87eb-2c674ea61e85" 17592186417368 "answer-693517ab-7974-5643-b63c-0b1e93f9bf86" 17592186417369 "answer-7e84734a-f76d-51fa-a6d7-e244eb448774" 17592186417370 "answer-8dbc9696-4140-550a-b72f-debd09d5fe0d" 17592186417371 "answer-932f9073-db7f-59db-843a-495c4d7ae